{"id": "EUVD-2026-103796", "enisaUuid": "d5d193ca-440f-3e65-80ce-078da2a5e54d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nkprobes: Skip disarmed probes when checking optkprobe overlap\n\nOn x86, an optkprobe at A replaces five bytes with a jump. If a disabled\nprobe B is at A+2, get_optimized_kprobe() stops at B when arming a new\nprobe C at A+4. It leaves A optimized:\n\n              A    A+1  A+2  A+3  A+4\n  A's jump  | e9 | d0 | d1 | d2 | d3 |\n  after C   | e9 | d0 | d1 | d2 | cc |\n\nThe INT3 for C overwrites the last byte of A's jump displacement, so\nexecution can jump to the wrong address. B can have prepared optinsns\nwhile disarmed, but has no jump to unoptimize.\n\nContinue past disarmed and unprepared probes to find the active optimized\nprobe before arming a probe in its jump.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f968dcdf018861129f97910fa7bd680d939a9b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/985a568171e7bdba6dcde3420d0e5bb515813457", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6745fa65f4115045431c0c15610e876855a04625", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/526fac219e8b7d3369b43026bd0a1df51b811cd4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a39c732a22ec4a369af9e19fbe3d666ec83eec4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98856", "GHSA-9hm5-vfv2-whh5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0259d35c-d78b-3027-b7e3-ef373adbcd91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "29dc1a18-3764-3e7e-b13d-0edf5b55d0f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3757f886-71b3-39ed-83e5-a077253cfea4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "afd66255b9a48f5851326ddae50e2203fbf71dc9 <526fac219e8b7d3369b43026bd0a1df51b811cd4"}, {"id": "40535dcb-2e9e-3ce9-9e3c-2cd60ab9111c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "afd66255b9a48f5851326ddae50e2203fbf71dc9 <7a39c732a22ec4a369af9e19fbe3d666ec83eec4"}, {"id": "55fba866-6d19-31e5-b1c0-c570254c1a72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.34"}, {"id": "56116a91-9858-313f-8138-ea9b33fdb0f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "64be2a37-1c45-3b37-8633-fcdee73e10ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "afd66255b9a48f5851326ddae50e2203fbf71dc9 <3f968dcdf018861129f97910fa7bd680d939a9b0"}, {"id": "8df20c64-0c8f-3c09-b3f6-776f367ab5a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "afd66255b9a48f5851326ddae50e2203fbf71dc9 <6745fa65f4115045431c0c15610e876855a04625"}, {"id": "9da1f025-2389-3836-a0ad-3a6b9675b061", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "af0871db-4401-3df1-9a83-32a045062fbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "b6072955-e7f3-393b-9d04-2bd612972724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e495ae90-e4cf-30d8-adc1-89c39971aebb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "afd66255b9a48f5851326ddae50e2203fbf71dc9 <985a568171e7bdba6dcde3420d0e5bb515813457"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d0add3b1-a0e2-34bf-bcca-93eb2d2468a2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}